// VoxelLandPolar.ush - The polar surfaces (stage T5d3, Design/LandClimate.md): the noise library's
// `polar` set laid where the planet's climate snapshot makes ice or frozen ground. Three of its
// channels, each a simulated heightfield in the set's texels:
//   R  crevasses: lens-shaped slots across the set's x (the ice's flow), en echelon
//   G  sastrugi: wind-cut snow ridges along x (the wind), on a flat floor
//   B  ice-wedge polygons: low-centred polygons with raised rims along their troughs (isotropic)
//   A  sea ice (stage T5e; not read here)
// Like the other climate layers this is geometry: applied after the rivers' and lakes' carve and
// the ice sheets (VoxelLandGully.ush VoxelLandSurfaceTermsDF), as more carve, so every host (the
// mesher, collision, the land cache, the ocean, the CPU queries) has it. Placed once per climate
// capture; it doesn't move with the seasons.
//
// WHERE (VoxelLandPolarSiteAt), from the climate cell at the sample and what the chain already
// knows there:
//   - the ice: the ice sheet's share (VoxelLandIce.ush's fade) and the glaciers' today (Now: the
//     glacial layer's own share, Ohmura's line at the bake's height, VoxelLandGlacialSiteAt's);
//   - CREVASSES where the ice runs steep: on the sheet where its own slope (Nye's profile, steepest
//     near the margin: K / 2h) passes 0.02 .. 0.08, so a marginal crevasse zone of a few to about
//     fifteen kilometres; on glaciers where the ground's large-scale slope (the bake's and the
//     layers' steering) passes 0.08 .. 0.3 (icefalls, steep tongues). Across the flow: the set's x
//     down the ice's slope (transverse crevasses);
//   - SASTRUGI on ice and snow that stay cold the year round (the year's mean at the surface from
//     -2 C to -10 C: dry snow), along the wind: the snapshot's sand drift (its lowest layer's
//     resultant, times its steadiness) plus, on the sheets' slopes, the katabatic wind: down the
//     slope, turned 40 degrees by the Coriolis force (to the right in the north, the left in the
//     south; Parish & Bromwich 1987: Antarctica's katabatics run 30 to 50 degrees off the fall
//     line). Where the two cancel or there's no wind, no sastrugi (no direction to lie along);
//   - SNOW DUNES on the flat snow plains (the ice sheets' thick interiors, cold flat glacier ice):
//     the dune set's G (rounded crests, across the wind) at a long spacing and a low height, the
//     megadunes and snow dunes of the polar plateaus (Fahnestock et al. 2000; Frezzotti et al. 2002:
//     a few metres high, kilometres apart, crests across the katabatic wind), sastrugi on them;
//   - ICE-WEDGE POLYGONS on bare (unglaciated) ground with continuous permafrost: the year's mean at
//     the ground from LandPolarPermafrostT + 2 C to - 2 C (Pewe 1966: active ice wedges need a
//     mean of about -6 C to -8 C or colder), on low slopes (0.04 .. 0.12 of the ground's
//     large-scale slope), inland (bake 1 .. 10 m) and outside the rivers and lakes.
//
// THE LATTICE: as the dunes' (VoxelLandDunes.ush): per face, the directed features take the two of
// VOXEL_LAND_DUNE_BINS fixed exact turns either side of their direction in the face's frame (less
// the set's own grain: polar_a's crevasses run about 27 degrees off its y, measured on the CPU) and
// blend them keeping the variance, over the middle 40% between two turns only (a crevasse field
// blended over all of it reads as two crossing sets); the polygons one turn per face (VoxelLandPeakRotation's) with
// any of the tile's 8 orientations. Faces blend as the set layers' (VoxelLandSetLayerDF), all
// zero-mean (each channel's mean over mip 0 subtracted: a coarse mip, a coarse footprint, flattens
// to nothing). One lookup call site in a loop (each call inlines the B-spline: the shaders' size).
//
// SCALE: each feature's texel is its spacing (one of the set's cells) over the set's cell in
// texels, its height the set's at that texel times its height scale (1: the simulated slopes).
// Band-limited by its mip level (texels about half the footprint, the dunes' rule) and faded out
// over the two levels before one cell fits a texel (VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FADE_LEVELS; skipped beyond).
//
// GRADIENT: the lookups' exact (B-spline) gradients at the amplitudes, plus each feature's unit
// times its amplitude's change where the chain knows it: the ice sheet's fade, the glaciers' share
// along the bake's slope, the temperature ramps and the coast through the bake's height. Left out
// (each changes over kilometres, or is a fade near a river): the slope gates, the wind's strength,
// the climate's own change between cells, and the rivers' and lakes' fades.
//
// Shared subset (VoxelShaderCompat.h). Included by VoxelLandGully.ush after VoxelLandIce.ush; its
// inputs, declared by the host:
//   LandClimate, LandHasClimate, LandClimateLapse   the climate (VoxelLandClimateAccess.ush)
//   uint LandPolarBase, LandPolarN, LandPolarMips;   the polar set's chain in LandNoise (0 size: none)
//   uint LandPolarSeed;
//   float LandPolarCrevasseTexelsPerCell;   R's mip-0 texels per bake cell (0: no crevasses)
//   float LandPolarCrevasseM;               m per unit value of R (its range x texel x height scale)
//   float LandPolarCrevasseMean;            R's mean over mip 0 (unit)
//   float LandPolarCrevasseFade;            the mip level by which it has faded out
//   float LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell, LandPolarSastrugiM, LandPolarSastrugiMean, LandPolarSastrugiFade;   G's
//   float LandPolarPolygonTexelsPerCell, LandPolarPolygonM, LandPolarPolygonMean, LandPolarPolygonFade;       B's
//   float LandPolarPermafrostT;             C: the year's mean at which the polygons are half in
//   float LandPolarCrevasseTurn;            radians: R's grain, its slots' normal from the set's x
//                                           (VoxelNoiseTiles::GrainAngleOf), turned onto the flow
//   float LandPolarSastrugiTurn;            radians: G's ridges' long axis from the set's x, turned
//                                           onto the wind
//   uint LandPolarDuneBase, LandPolarDuneN, LandPolarDuneMips;   the dune set's chain (the snow
//                                           dunes: its G, x downwind; 0 size: none)
//   float LandPolarDuneTexelsPerCell, LandPolarDuneM, LandPolarDuneMean, LandPolarDuneFade;   its G's

#ifndef VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_USH
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_USH

#include "VoxelLandPeaks.ush"
#include "VoxelLandDunes.ush"
#include "VoxelLandClimateAccess.ush"

// The sheet's own slope (m/m) over which crevasses come in (Nye: 0.08 about 140 m thick, 0.02
// about 560 m: within about 1 and 14 km of the margin).
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SHEET_SLOPE_START 0.02f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SHEET_SLOPE_END 0.08f
// The ground's large-scale slope over which glaciers crevasse (about 5 to 17 degrees).
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_GLACIER_SLOPE_START 0.08f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_GLACIER_SLOPE_END 0.3f
// The year's mean at the surface (C) over which the snow is dry enough for sastrugi.
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SASTRUGI_WARM -2.0f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SASTRUGI_COLD -10.0f
// The katabatic wind: the sheet's slope over which it comes in, and its turn off the fall line
// (radians: 40 degrees), and the wind's strength (drift steadiness plus katabatic share) over which
// the sastrugi come in.
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_KATABATIC_START 0.001f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_KATABATIC_END 0.004f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_KATABATIC_TURN 0.6981317f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_WIND_START 0.05f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_WIND_END 0.3f
// The polygons: half the ramp about LandPolarPermafrostT (C), the slopes over which they go, the
// bake heights over which they come in from the coast.
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PERMAFROST_HALF 2.0f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLAT_START 0.04f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLAT_END 0.12f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_COAST_START 1.0f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_COAST_END 10.0f
// The snow plains: the sheet's own slope (m/m) over which its plain gives way (Nye: 0.005 about
// 2 km thick, 0.02 about 550 m), and the ground's over which a glacier's does.
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_SHEET_START 0.005f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_SHEET_END 0.02f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_LAND_START 0.02f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_LAND_END 0.06f
// The bake's height (m) over which the glaciers' ice comes in from the sea (as the ice sheets':
// VoxelLandIce.ush's VOXEL_LAND_ICE_LAND_M; none on the sea floor), and the share of the two flows'
// weights their sum keeps under which crevasses give way (where a glacier's and a sheet's flows
// cancel the direction means little).
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_LAND_M 20.0f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLOW_START 0.1f
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLOW_END 0.4f
// The mip levels over which a feature fades out before its cell fits one texel.
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FADE_LEVELS 2.0f
// Half the share of a turn's span (22.5 degrees) over which the two turns either side of a
// direction blend (the dunes blend over all of it): elsewhere one turn shows alone, so a crevasse
// field or the sastrugi read as one set, not two crossing ones.
#define VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_TURN_BLEND 0.2f

/** Whether the planet has polar surfaces (the set, any feature placed, a climate). */
VOXEL_FUNC bool VoxelLandPolarOn(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS_DECL float Dummy)
{
    return LandPolarN != 0u && LandHasClimate != 0u
        && (LandPolarCrevasseTexelsPerCell > 0.0f || LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell > 0.0f || LandPolarPolygonTexelsPerCell > 0.0f
            || (LandPolarDuneTexelsPerCell > 0.0f && LandPolarDuneN != 0u));
}

/** The features' shares at a sample (0..1) and directions (unit tangents at the point, planet
 *  frame; zero where there's none), and the shares' gradients where the chain knows them (per m,
 *  tangent). */
struct FVoxelLandPolarSite
{
    float Crevasse;
    float Sastrugi;
    float Polygon;
    float SnowDune;
    float3 Flow;
    float3 Wind;
    float3 CrevasseGradient;
    float3 SastrugiGradient;
    float3 PolygonGradient;
    float3 SnowDuneGradient;
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelLandPolarSite VoxelLandPolarNone()
{
    FVoxelLandPolarSite Out;
    Out.Crevasse = 0.0f;
    Out.Sastrugi = 0.0f;
    Out.Polygon = 0.0f;
    Out.SnowDune = 0.0f;
    Out.Flow = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    Out.Wind = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    Out.CrevasseGradient = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    Out.SastrugiGradient = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    Out.PolygonGradient = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    Out.SnowDuneGradient = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    return Out;
}

/** V (a tangent vector at the unit direction Up) turned by Angle (radians) about Up: positive to
 *  the left (counter-clockwise seen from above). */
VOXEL_FUNC float3 VoxelLandPolarTurn(float3 V, float3 Up, float Angle)
{
    return V * cos(Angle) + cross(Up, V) * sin(Angle);
}

/** The site at the unit direction Normal: the bake's height (m) and gradient (m/m, tangent), the
 *  ground's large-scale gradient (the bake's plus the layers' steering), the surface's height (m:
 *  the snow's temperature), the ice sheet's share of the surface (FVoxelLandIceSurface::Cover),
 *  own slope (its surface without the swells: m/m, tangent) and the share's
 *  gradient (bGradients), and the rivers' and lakes' keep (1 off them). */
VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelLandPolarSite VoxelLandPolarSiteAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS_DECL float3 Normal, float Bake, float3 BakeGradient, float3 LandSteer,
    float Surface, float IceFade, float3 IceSlope, float3 IceFadeGradient, float WaterKeep, bool bGradients)
{
    FVoxelLandPolarSite Out = VoxelLandPolarNone();
    if (!VoxelLandPolarOn(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS 0.0f)) return Out;
    const FVoxelLandClimateTaps Taps = VoxelLandClimateTapsOf(Normal);
    const FVoxelLandClimateCell Cell = VoxelLandClimateCellAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS Taps);
    // The temperature's change per m of the bake's height (0 under the sea, where it's clamped).
    const float DTDH = Bake > 0.0f ? -LandClimateLapse * 0.001f : 0.0f;

    // The glaciers today, as the glacial layer's (VoxelLandGlacialSiteAt) at the bake's height.
    const float GW = VOXEL_LAND_GLACIAL_WIDTH;
    const float Margin = VoxelLandClimateGlacierMargin(Cell, LandClimateLapse, Bake, 0.0f);
    // On land only (review fix: the sea floor under a cold sea read as glacier ice), and out of the
    // rivers and lakes.
    const float LandShare = smoothstep(0.0f, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_LAND_M, Bake);
    const float NowRamp = VoxelLandClimateRamp(-GW, GW, Margin);
    const float Now = NowRamp * LandShare * WaterKeep;
    const float3 NowGradient = BakeGradient * ((VoxelLandGlacialFadeSlope(-GW, GW, Margin) * -DTDH * LandShare
        + NowRamp * VoxelLandGlacialFadeSlope(0.0f, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_LAND_M, Bake)) * WaterKeep);
    // T5e: the ice shelf (raised in the bake, VoxelLandShelf.h; its share the map's at the bake's
    // height, VoxelLandClimateShelfOf), out of the rivers and lakes.
    const FVoxelLandClimateShelf ShelfOf = VoxelLandClimateShelfOf(Cell, Bake);
    const float Shelf = ShelfOf.Share * WaterKeep;
    const float3 ShelfGradient = BakeGradient * (ShelfOf.Slope * WaterKeep);
    // The ice on the ground: a glacier or the shelf.
    const float Ground = Now + Shelf - Now * Shelf;
    const float3 GroundGradient = NowGradient * (1.0f - Shelf) + ShelfGradient * (1.0f - Now);
    // The ice cover: the sheet, a glacier or the shelf.
    const float Iced = Ground + IceFade - Ground * IceFade;
    const float3 IcedGradient = GroundGradient * (1.0f - IceFade) + IceFadeGradient * (1.0f - Ground);
    const float SteerSlope = length(LandSteer);
    const float SheetSlope = length(IceSlope);

    // Crevasses: glaciers on steep ground, and the sheet near its margin; across the ice's flow.
    if (LandPolarCrevasseTexelsPerCell > 0.0f && Iced > 0.0f)
    {
        const float GS = smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_GLACIER_SLOPE_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_GLACIER_SLOPE_END, SteerSlope);
        const float SS = smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SHEET_SLOPE_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SHEET_SLOPE_END, SheetSlope);
        const float Gc = Now * (1.0f - IceFade) * GS;
        const float Sc = IceFade * SS;
        float3 Flow = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
        if (Gc > 0.0f && SteerSlope > 1.0e-6f) Flow = Flow - LandSteer * (Gc / SteerSlope);
        if (Sc > 0.0f && SheetSlope > 1.0e-6f) Flow = Flow - IceSlope * (Sc / SheetSlope);
        const float FlowLength = length(Flow);
        // Where the two flows cancel, the crevasses give way (their direction means little there).
        const float Agree = smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLOW_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLOW_END, FlowLength / max(Gc + Sc, 1.0e-6f));
        if (FlowLength > 1.0e-6f && Agree > 0.0f)
        {
            Out.Flow = Flow / FlowLength;
            Out.Crevasse = (Gc + Sc - Gc * Sc) * Agree;
            if (bGradients)
            {
                const float3 GcGradient = (NowGradient * (1.0f - IceFade) - IceFadeGradient * Now) * GS;
                const float3 ScGradient = IceFadeGradient * SS;
                Out.CrevasseGradient = (GcGradient * (1.0f - Sc) + ScGradient * (1.0f - Gc)) * Agree;
            }
        }
    }

    // Sastrugi and snow dunes: cold ice and snow, along the wind.
    const bool bSnowDunes = LandPolarDuneTexelsPerCell > 0.0f && LandPolarDuneN != 0u;
    if ((LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell > 0.0f || bSnowDunes) && Iced > 0.0f)
    {
        // At the surface's own height (the ice's top on a sheet).
        const float T = Cell.SeaTemperature - LandClimateLapse * max(Surface, 0.0f) * 0.001f;
        const float Cold = VoxelLandClimateRamp(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SASTRUGI_WARM, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SASTRUGI_COLD, T);
        if (Cold > 0.0f)
        {
            // The drift (east and north at the point, Z the spin axis), times its steadiness.
            const float3 Drift = VoxelLandClimateDriftAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS Taps);
            float3 Wind = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
            const float3 EastRaw = float3(-Normal.y, Normal.x, 0.0f);
            const float EastLength = length(EastRaw);
            const float DriftLength = sqrt(Drift.x * Drift.x + Drift.y * Drift.y);
            if (EastLength > 1.0e-4f && DriftLength > 1.0e-4f)
            {
                const float3 East = EastRaw / EastLength;
                const float3 North = cross(Normal, East);
                Wind = (East * Drift.x + North * Drift.y) * (saturate(Drift.z) / DriftLength);
            }
            // The katabatic wind down the sheet's slope, turned by the Coriolis force (to the right
            // in the north: a negative turn; smoothly through the equator, where no sheet is).
            if (IceFade > 0.0f && SheetSlope > 1.0e-6f)
            {
                const float K = IceFade * smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_KATABATIC_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_KATABATIC_END, SheetSlope);
                const float Hemisphere = clamp(Normal.z * 10.0f, -1.0f, 1.0f);
                Wind = Wind + VoxelLandPolarTurn(IceSlope * (-1.0f / SheetSlope), Normal, -VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_KATABATIC_TURN * Hemisphere) * K;
            }
            const float WindLength = length(Wind);
            const float WindShare = smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_WIND_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_WIND_END, WindLength);
            if (WindShare > 0.0f)
            {
                Out.Wind = Wind / WindLength;
                // The cold's change with the bake's height (the sheet's thickness left out).
                const float3 ColdGradient = BakeGradient * (VoxelLandGlacialFadeSlope(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SASTRUGI_WARM, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_SASTRUGI_COLD, T) * DTDH);
                if (LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell > 0.0f)
                {
                    Out.Sastrugi = Iced * Cold * WindShare;
                    if (bGradients)
                        Out.SastrugiGradient = (IcedGradient * Cold + ColdGradient * Iced) * WindShare;
                }
                if (bSnowDunes)
                {
                    // The snow plains: the sheet's thick, flat interior, flat glacier ice or the ice
                    // shelf (T5e); out of the crevasses.
                    const float FlatSheet = 1.0f - smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_SHEET_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_SHEET_END, SheetSlope);
                    const float FlatLand = 1.0f - smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_LAND_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PLAIN_LAND_END, SteerSlope);
                    const float Plain = IceFade * FlatSheet + Ground * (1.0f - IceFade) * FlatLand;
                    const float Open = 1.0f - Out.Crevasse;
                    Out.SnowDune = Plain * Cold * WindShare * Open;
                    if (bGradients)
                    {
                        const float3 PlainGradient = IceFadeGradient * (FlatSheet - Ground * FlatLand) + GroundGradient * ((1.0f - IceFade) * FlatLand);
                        Out.SnowDuneGradient = ((PlainGradient * Cold + ColdGradient * Plain) * Open - Out.CrevasseGradient * (Plain * Cold)) * WindShare;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // Ice-wedge polygons: bare frozen ground, flat, inland, out of the water.
    if (LandPolarPolygonTexelsPerCell > 0.0f && Iced < 1.0f && WaterKeep > 0.0f)
    {
        const float T = Cell.SeaTemperature - LandClimateLapse * max(Bake, 0.0f) * 0.001f;
        const float TWarm = LandPolarPermafrostT + VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PERMAFROST_HALF;
        const float TCold = LandPolarPermafrostT - VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_PERMAFROST_HALF;
        const float Frozen = VoxelLandClimateRamp(TWarm, TCold, T);
        const float Coast = smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_COAST_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_COAST_END, Bake);
        const float Flat = 1.0f - smoothstep(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLAT_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FLAT_END, SteerSlope);
        const float Bare = 1.0f - Iced;
        Out.Polygon = Bare * Frozen * Coast * Flat * WaterKeep;
        if (bGradients && Out.Polygon > 0.0f)
        {
            const float3 FrozenGradient = BakeGradient * (VoxelLandGlacialFadeSlope(TWarm, TCold, T) * DTDH);
            const float3 CoastGradient = BakeGradient * VoxelLandGlacialFadeSlope(VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_COAST_START, VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_COAST_END, Bake);
            Out.PolygonGradient = (IcedGradient * (-Frozen * Coast) + FrozenGradient * (Bare * Coast) + CoastGradient * (Bare * Frozen)) * (Flat * WaterKeep);
        }
    }
    return Out;
}

/** The polar surfaces' height (m) and gradient (m/m, tangent at the point; bGradients). */
struct FVoxelLandPolar
{
    float Height;
    float3 Gradient;
};

/** A feature's footprint fade: 1 until VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FADE_LEVELS before Fade, 0 from Fade (its
 *  mip level from the footprint, cm, and its texel, m: texels about half the footprint). */
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelLandPolarFadeOf(float Footprint, float TexelM, float Fade)
{
    const float Level = max(log2(max(Footprint, 1.0f) / (TexelM * 100.0f)) - 1.0f, 0.0f);
    return 1.0f - smoothstep(Fade - VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_FADE_LEVELS, Fade, Level);
}

/** The bin either side of a direction's angle in a face's frame, less Turn (radians: the set's own
 *  grain, so the set's slots or ridges, not its x, end up across or along the direction): the
 *  lower bin and the share of the upper (Tw: sharpened to VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_TURN_BLEND about the
 *  middle). */
struct FVoxelLandPolarBins
{
    uint B0;
    uint B1;
    float Tw;
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelLandPolarBins VoxelLandPolarBinsOf(float3 Dir, FVoxelLandFaceFrame Frame, float Turn)
{
    const float WU = dot(Dir, normalize(Frame.TU));
    const float WV = dot(Dir, normalize(Frame.TV));
    float Phi = ((WU * WU + WV * WV > 1.0e-8f ? atan2(WV, WU) : 0.0f) - Turn) * (float(VOXEL_LAND_DUNE_BINS) / 6.28318531f);
    // (atan2 within -pi .. pi, Turn within -pi/2 .. pi/2: one wrap is enough.)
    if (Phi < 0.0f) Phi += float(VOXEL_LAND_DUNE_BINS);
    const float Floor = floor(Phi);
    FVoxelLandPolarBins Out;
    Out.Tw = smoothstep(0.5f - VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_TURN_BLEND, 0.5f + VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_TURN_BLEND, Phi - Floor);
    Out.B0 = uint(Floor) % VOXEL_LAND_DUNE_BINS;
    Out.B1 = (Out.B0 + 1u) % VOXEL_LAND_DUNE_BINS;
    return Out;
}

/** The polar surfaces at the sea-level sphere point P (double-float, cm) for a site
 *  (VoxelLandPolarSiteAt), band-limited to Footprint (cm). Zero-mean features, each within its
 *  channel's range about its mean times sqrt 2 (the two turns) times the face blend's bound
 *  (VoxelLand::PolarReach). */
VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelLandPolar VoxelLandPolarDF(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS_DECL float2 PX, float2 PY, float2 PZ, FVoxelLandPolarSite Site, float Footprint,
    bool bGradients)
{
    FVoxelLandPolar Out;
    Out.Height = 0.0f;
    Out.Gradient = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    // Each feature's texel (m), amplitude (m per unit value: its share, its scale, its footprint
    // fade) and the amplitude's gradient.
    const float TexelC = LandPolarCrevasseTexelsPerCell > 0.0f ? LandCellM / LandPolarCrevasseTexelsPerCell : 1.0f;
    const float TexelS = LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell > 0.0f ? LandCellM / LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell : 1.0f;
    const float TexelP = LandPolarPolygonTexelsPerCell > 0.0f ? LandCellM / LandPolarPolygonTexelsPerCell : 1.0f;
    const float TexelD = LandPolarDuneTexelsPerCell > 0.0f ? LandCellM / LandPolarDuneTexelsPerCell : 1.0f;
    const float MC = Site.Crevasse > 0.0f ? LandPolarCrevasseM * VoxelLandPolarFadeOf(Footprint, TexelC, LandPolarCrevasseFade) : 0.0f;
    const float MS = Site.Sastrugi > 0.0f ? LandPolarSastrugiM * VoxelLandPolarFadeOf(Footprint, TexelS, LandPolarSastrugiFade) : 0.0f;
    const float MP = Site.Polygon > 0.0f ? LandPolarPolygonM * VoxelLandPolarFadeOf(Footprint, TexelP, LandPolarPolygonFade) : 0.0f;
    const float MD = Site.SnowDune > 0.0f ? LandPolarDuneM * VoxelLandPolarFadeOf(Footprint, TexelD, LandPolarDuneFade) : 0.0f;
    const float AC = Site.Crevasse * MC;
    const float AS = Site.Sastrugi * MS;
    const float AP = Site.Polygon * MP;
    const float AD = Site.SnowDune * MD;
    if (AC <= 0.0f && AS <= 0.0f && AP <= 0.0f && AD <= 0.0f) return Out;

    const float Band = 2.0f * VOXEL_LAND_PEAK_BAND_CELLS / float(LandN);
    const float DSDX = 2.0f / (float(LandN) * LandCellM);
    const FVoxelLandNoiseSetRef PolarSet = VoxelLandNoiseSetOf(LandPolarBase, LandPolarN, LandPolarMips);
    const FVoxelLandNoiseSetRef DuneSet = VoxelLandNoiseSetOf(LandPolarDuneBase, LandPolarDuneN, LandPolarDuneMips);
    float WSum = 0.0f;
    float W2Sum = 0.0f;
    float USum = 0.0f;       // sum of W x the face's height (m)
    float UCSum = 0.0f;      // per feature, sum of W x the face's unit (the amplitudes' change)
    float USSum = 0.0f;
    float UPSum = 0.0f;
    float UDSum = 0.0f;
    float3 GSum = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    float3 WWGrad = float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    VOXEL_LOOP
    for (uint Axis = 0u; Axis < 3u; Axis++)
    {
        const float2 PN = VoxelLandPick(PX, PY, PZ, Axis);
        if (PN.x == 0.0f) continue;
        const bool bNegative = PN.x < 0.0f;
        const uint Face = Axis * 2u + (bNegative ? 1u : 0u);
        const float2 Den = bNegative ? float2(-PN.x, -PN.y) : PN;
        const float2 AU = VoxelDFDiv(VoxelLandPick(PX, PY, PZ, VoxelCubeUAxis(Face)), Den);
        const float2 AV = VoxelDFDiv(VoxelLandPick(PX, PY, PZ, VoxelCubeVAxis(Face)), Den);
        const float S = atan(AU.x) * VOXEL_LAND_INV_QUARTER_PI;
        const float T = atan(AV.x) * VOXEL_LAND_INV_QUARTER_PI;
        const float RS = VoxelLandFaceRamp(S, Band);
        const float RT = VoxelLandFaceRamp(T, Band);
        const float W = RS * RT;
        if (W <= 0.0f) continue;
        const FVoxelLandFaceFrame Frame = VoxelLandFaceFrameAt(Face, AU.x, AV.x);
        const FVoxelLandPeakCoord CU = VoxelLandPeakCoordAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS VoxelLandAxisAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS AU, S));
        const FVoxelLandPeakCoord CV = VoxelLandPeakCoordAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS VoxelLandAxisAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS AV, T));
        // The directed features' turns either side of their directions, their weights over the
        // root of their squares (the variance kept: one turn's own at Tw 0 or 1).
        const FVoxelLandPolarBins BC = VoxelLandPolarBinsOf(Site.Flow, Frame, LandPolarCrevasseTurn);
        const FVoxelLandPolarBins BS = VoxelLandPolarBinsOf(Site.Wind, Frame, LandPolarSastrugiTurn);
        const float QC = 1.0f / sqrt((1.0f - BC.Tw) * (1.0f - BC.Tw) + BC.Tw * BC.Tw);
        const float QS = 1.0f / sqrt((1.0f - BS.Tw) * (1.0f - BS.Tw) + BS.Tw * BS.Tw);
        const FVoxelLandPolarBins BD = VoxelLandPolarBinsOf(Site.Wind, Frame, 0.0f);
        const float QD = 1.0f / sqrt((1.0f - BD.Tw) * (1.0f - BD.Tw) + BD.Tw * BD.Tw);
        float FaceU = 0.0f;
        float FaceUC = 0.0f;
        float FaceUS = 0.0f;
        float FaceUP = 0.0f;
        float FaceUD = 0.0f;
        float FaceGU = 0.0f;
        float FaceGV = 0.0f;
        // The taps: the crevasses' two turns, the sastrugi's two, the polygons' one, the snow dunes'
        // two (the wind's turns: the dune set's x is downwind, its crests across it). One lookup
        // call site.
        VOXEL_LOOP
        for (uint Tap = 0u; Tap < 7u; Tap++)
        {
            const uint Feature = Tap < 2u ? 0u : (Tap < 4u ? 1u : (Tap < 5u ? 2u : 3u));
            FVoxelLandNoiseSetRef Set = PolarSet;
            float A = AP;
            float Weight = 1.0f;
            uint Bin = 0u;
            float TPC = LandPolarPolygonTexelsPerCell;
            float Mean = LandPolarPolygonMean;
            uint Salt = 0x706f6c79u;
            if (Feature == 0u)
            {
                A = AC;
                Weight = (Tap == 0u ? 1.0f - BC.Tw : BC.Tw) * QC;
                Bin = Tap == 0u ? BC.B0 : BC.B1;
                TPC = LandPolarCrevasseTexelsPerCell;
                Mean = LandPolarCrevasseMean;
                Salt = 0x63726576u;
            }
            else if (Feature == 1u)
            {
                A = AS;
                Weight = (Tap == 2u ? 1.0f - BS.Tw : BS.Tw) * QS;
                Bin = Tap == 2u ? BS.B0 : BS.B1;
                TPC = LandPolarSastrugiTexelsPerCell;
                Mean = LandPolarSastrugiMean;
                Salt = 0x73617374u;
            }
            else if (Feature == 3u)
            {
                A = AD;
                // The dune set's own x (no grain turn): the wind's turns before the sastrugi's grain.
                Weight = (Tap == 5u ? 1.0f - BD.Tw : BD.Tw) * QD;
                Bin = Tap == 5u ? BD.B0 : BD.B1;
                TPC = LandPolarDuneTexelsPerCell;
                Mean = LandPolarDuneMean;
                Salt = 0x736e6f77u;
                Set = DuneSet;
            }
            if (A <= 0.0f || Weight <= 0.0f) continue;
            const uint H = VoxelHash(uint3(Face, Bin, Salt), LandPolarSeed);
            const uint H2 = VoxelHash(uint3(Face, Bin, Salt ^ 0x5f5f5f5fu), LandPolarSeed);
            // The directed features: the bin's turn, the set as it is (a mirror would turn its grain
            // the other way); the polygons: the face's own turn, any orientation.
            float2 Rot = VoxelLandDuneRotation(Bin);
            uint Orient = 0u;
            if (Feature == 2u)
            {
                Rot = VoxelLandPeakRotation(H >> 29u);
                Orient = H & 7u;
            }
            // x = u cos + v sin, y = -u sin + v cos, in the set's texels.
            const FVoxelLandNoiseAxis AX = VoxelLandPeakRotated(CU, CV, Rot.x * TPC, Rot.y * TPC);
            const FVoxelLandNoiseAxis AY = VoxelLandPeakRotated(CU, CV, -Rot.y * TPC, Rot.x * TPC);
            const float TexelM = LandCellM / TPC;
            const float Level = max(log2(max(Footprint, 1.0f) / (TexelM * 100.0f)) - 1.0f, 0.0f);
            const FVoxelLandNoise N = VoxelLandNoiseAt(VOXEL_LAND_ARGS Set, AX, AY, Orient, H >> 3u, H2, Level,
                Feature == 2u ? VOXEL_LAND_NOISE_WANT_ONLY_B : 0u);
            float V = N.B;
            float VX = N.BU;
            float VY = N.BV;
            if (Feature == 0u)
            {
                V = N.R;
                VX = N.RU;
                VY = N.RV;
            }
            else if (Feature != 2u)
            {
                // The sastrugi, and the snow dunes (the dune set's G, rounded crests).
                V = N.G;
                VX = N.GU;
                VY = N.GV;
            }
            const float Unit = (V - Mean) * Weight;
            FaceU += Unit * A;
            if (Feature == 0u) FaceUC += Unit;
            else if (Feature == 1u) FaceUS += Unit;
            else if (Feature == 2u) FaceUP += Unit;
            else FaceUD += Unit;
            // Back to the face's axes (per m): d/du = cos d/dx - sin d/dy, d/dv = sin d/dx + cos d/dy.
            const float S2 = Weight * A / TexelM;
            FaceGU += (Rot.x * VX - Rot.y * VY) * S2;
            FaceGV += (Rot.y * VX + Rot.x * VY) * S2;
        }
        // The faces as the set layers', about zero.
        const float WSU = VoxelLandFaceRampSlope(S, Band) * RT * DSDX;
        const float WSV = RS * VoxelLandFaceRampSlope(T, Band) * DSDX;
        USum += W * FaceU;
        UCSum += W * FaceUC;
        USSum += W * FaceUS;
        UPSum += W * FaceUP;
        UDSum += W * FaceUD;
        WSum += W;
        W2Sum += W * W;
        if (bGradients)
        {
            GSum = GSum + VoxelLandFaceVector(Frame, W * FaceGU + FaceU * WSU, W * FaceGV + FaceU * WSV);
            WWGrad = WWGrad + VoxelLandFaceVector(Frame, W * WSU, W * WSV);
        }
    }
    if (WSum <= 0.0f) return Out;
    const float InvQ = 1.0f / sqrt(W2Sum);
    Out.Height = USum * InvQ;
    if (bGradients)
    {
        const float InvQ3 = InvQ * InvQ * InvQ;
        // The shape at fixed amplitudes, then each feature's unit times its amplitude's change.
        Out.Gradient = GSum * InvQ - WWGrad * (USum * InvQ3)
            + Site.CrevasseGradient * (UCSum * InvQ * MC) + Site.SastrugiGradient * (USSum * InvQ * MS) + Site.PolygonGradient * (UPSum * InvQ * MP)
            + Site.SnowDuneGradient * (UDSum * InvQ * MD);
    }
    return Out;
}

#endif // VOXEL_LAND_POLAR_USH
